# PSR-5h — dual-store cleanup (classification wave)

## PSR-5 item 6 intent

> dual storeهایی که تنها برای scaffold مانده‌اند حذف یا **صریحاً test adapter** شوند.

Production/prodlike already refuse memory via `assertProductionStorageDriver`
(PSR-5a). This wave answers: which of the ten factories are scaffold-only
deletion candidates vs intentional test|dev adapters?

## Decision (inventory)

**Zero scaffold-only deletion candidates** in this release.

All ten factories are classified
`retained_explicit_test_dev_adapter`:

| Domain | Evidence |
| --- | --- |
| bookings / identity | `createWithDevSeed` + `reset*ForTests` + active specs |
| tour_storage | dedicated smoke memory stores + many specs |
| portal_member_plan | `setPortalMemberPlanRepositoryForTests` + broad refs |
| settings ×3 / drafts ×2 | `reset*ForTests` + factory InMemory branch |
| finance | `resetFinanceRepositoryForTests` + recon/service specs |

Deleting InMemory now would break local/dev and large test surface without
improving production posture (already fail-closed).

## Code ratchet (minimal)

`apps/api/src/storage/dual-store-role.ts` exports
`DUAL_STORE_ROLE_RETAINED_TEST_DEV_ADAPTER`.

Each of the ten factories re-exports:

```ts
export const DUAL_STORE_ROLE = DUAL_STORE_ROLE_RETAINED_TEST_DEV_ADAPTER;
```

No driver / assert / InMemory algorithm changes.

## Non-goals

- Removing any InMemory implementation
- Same-SHA migration/RLS/outbox proofs (item 7)
- Changing `STORAGE_DRIVER` resolution

## Item 6 status after this wave

**Complete for classification + explicit adapter marking.** Future prisma-only
narrowing requires Architect YES and a dedicated deletion wave per domain.

## Smoke

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-5h-dual-store-smoke.mjs
node scripts/ops/psr-5-data-authority-inventory-smoke.mjs
```
